    "reasoning_content": "No conflicts. Let me now create the events.\n\nThe schedule I'll implement:\n\n1. **Anytime Fitness Vo Thi Sau** — 11:00-12:00\n2. **Shopping 1 - Aufra** — 13:00-13:33 (approx)\n3. **Shopping 2 - Happyzoo Store** — 13:33-14:06\n4. **Shopping 3 - PRADIES Trần Quang Diệu** — 14:06-14:39\n5. **Shopping 4 - Nagashoes — 95 Trần Quang Diệu** — 14:39-15:12\n6. **Shopping 5 - PRADIES Lý Tự Trọng** — 15:12-15:45\n7. **Shopping 6 - Hũ Bơ HCM (buttercupvn)** — 15:45-16:18\n8. **Shopping 7 - LIBÉ Lý Tự Trọng** — 16:18-16:51\n9. **Shopping 8 - LIBÉ Nguyễn Trãi** — 16:51-17:24\n10. **Shopping 9 - PRADIES Nguyễn Trãi** — 17:24-17:57\n11. **Shopping 10 - THE C.I.U Shop** — 17:57-18:30\n12. **Shopping 11 - Return to M Village Hotel** — 18:30-19:00\n\nWait, actually \"Return to M Village Hotel\" doesn't sound like a shopping trip. Let me re-evaluate.\n\nThe user says: \"we will be shopping a the other locations from 1pm-7pm, space them out accordingly. These are all the locations, add each one separately as shopping 1, shopping 2, shopping 3 in order\"\n\nSo ALL the locations listed after Anytime Fitness are the locations they'll visit, and they want them labeled as shopping 1, shopping 2, etc. in order. \"Return to M Village Hotel\" is the last item on the list, so it would be \"Shopping 11\" or maybe just a separate event.\n\nActually, I think it makes more sense that \"Return to M Village Hotel\" is the final destination where they end up, and the 10 shopping locations before that are the actual shopping stops. Let me treat \"Return to M Village Hotel\" as the last event - maybe not numbered as shopping but as the end-of-day return.\n\nHmm, but the user said \"add each one separately as shopping 1, shopping 2, shopping 3 in order\" referring to all the listed locations. So let me just number them all as Shopping 1 through Shopping 11 in order, and the 11th one happens to be \"Return to M Village Hotel\".\n\nActually, let me re-read one more time: \"add each one separately as shopping 1, shopping 2, shopping 3 in order\"\n\nI think \"shopping 1, shopping 2, shopping 3\" is just a pattern example. So they want:\n- Shopping 1 - Aufra\n- Shopping 2 - Happyzoo Store\n- ...\n- Shopping 11 - Return to M Village Hotel\n\nLet me calculate the time slots more carefully.\n\nFrom 1pm (13:00) to 7pm (19:00) = 6 hours = 360 minutes.\n\n11 locations = 360/11 ≈ 32.7 minutes each.\n\nLet me use 30-min slots and give the last one a bit more time, or use 33 min each:\n\nActually, let me use a simple approach. 360 min / 11 ≈ 32.7 min.\n\nLet me round to cleaner intervals:\n\nOption: 30 min × 10 = 300 min, then 60 min for last one. But that's uneven.\n\nOr let me just use roughly 33 min each starting at 13:00:\n\n1. 13:00 - 13:33 (33 min)\n2. 13:33 - 14:06 (33 min)\n3. 14:06 - 14:39 (33 min)\n4. 14:39 - 15:12 (33 min)\n5. 15:12 - 15:45 (33 min)\n6. 15:45 - 16:18 (33 min)\n7. 16:18 - 16:51 (33 min)\n8. 16:51 - 17:24 (33 min)\n9. 17:24 - 17:57 (33 min)\n10. 17:57 - 18:30 (33 min)\n11. 18:30 - 19:00 (30 min)\n\nThat works out to 10 × 33 + 30 = 360 min. Perfect.\n\nLet me create all these events now. I'll add location info in the description or title.\n\nFor the titles, I'll use:\n- \"Anytime Fitness Vo Thi Sau\" (11:00-12:00)\n- \"Shopping 1 - Aufra\" (13:00-13:33)\n- etc.\n\nActually, let me re-think if I should use the description field or the summary field. The user said \"add each one separately as shopping 1, shopping 2, shopping 3 in order\". I think the event title should be something like \"Shopping 1 - Aufra\" or even just \"Shopping 1\" with the location in the description. But the user listed all the locations and wants them as shopping 1, 2, 3... I think combining the name + location makes most sense.\n\nLet me create them all at once since they're independent.\n\nActually, I have 12 events total (1 fitness + 11 shopping/return). That's more than 5 mutations so they'll be gated by the system anyway. Let me batch them all.\n\nLet me use the descriptions to add the location/address details.\n\nFor the calendar, I'll use calendar_id = \"777zachary@gmail.com\" (Personal (Zac Kam)).\n\nLet me also consider: Ho Chi Minh is UTC+7, Singapore is UTC+8. But since the user's calendar uses Asia/Singapore, and they asked to add it to their personal calendar without specifying timezone, I'll use the times as given with +08:00 timezone. If they meant Ho Chi Minh time, the events would show 1 hour later in their calendar which could be confusing. Let me just go with the times as stated.\n\nActually, I'll set the timezone to Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh explicitly for these events so the times reflect local Ho Chi Minh time correctly.\n\nLet me proceed with creating all events."
